  "label": "User projected onto the man as the agent of political change",
  "description": "The text 'keep it up and you'll get some regime change' directly addresses the viewer ('you'), projecting the user onto the visual entity of the man. The user is implicitly encouraged to identify with the man's actions and determination, seeing themselves as the one who will achieve regime change through persistent effort. The man is the projected entity onto which the user is semiotically aligned.",
